# Project 5: Data Cleaning & Transformation Using Power Query

## Project Overview
This project demonstrates how to clean, transform, merge, and append raw sales datasets using Microsoft Excel Power Query. It focuses on preparing reliable, structured data for business analysis and reporting.

## Project Objectives
- Import multiple raw datasets into Power Query.
- Remove blank rows and duplicate records.
- Trim extra spaces and standardize text formatting.
- Correct column names and data types.
- Identify and handle missing values and errors.
- Merge datasets using Order ID.
- Append multiple datasets into one consolidated table.
- Apply Unpivot to transform data from wide to long format.
- Load cleaned data into the Excel Data Model.
- Create PivotTables for sales analysis.

## Workbook Structure

| Worksheet / Query | Description |
|---|---|
| Raw Sales Data 1 | First source sales dataset |
| Raw Sales Data 2 | Second source sales dataset |
| Cleaned Sales Data | Merged and appended cleaned sales records |
| Unpivoted Data | Monthly sales data transformed into rows |
| Pivot Report | Sales analysis by region and product |

